By the fundamental theorem of calculus,

$
  (dif H(x))/(dif x) = delta(x).
$

Integrating once more gives the ramp function $r(x) = integral_0^x H(x') dif x'$, equal to $0$ for $x < 0$ and $x$ for $x >= 0$. Functions get smoother as they are integrated: the discontinuous Heaviside function integrates the distribution $delta$.
